{"memo": "\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nALDERMOOR INDUSTRIES \u2014 CFO AUDIT MEMORANDUM\nDate: 20 May 2024\nRE: Procurement Request Audit Summary\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nA multi-disciplinary audit of the \u20ac150,000 procurement order for 40 tonnes of precision steel components from JSC Rosoboronexport has concluded with a fatal compliance failure. While Group Treasury noted zero FX variance and Financial Control mapped the transaction to IAS 2 (GL 5xxx Raw Materials), the order breaches mandatory international sanctions and statutory import bans. Pursuant to Aldermoor\u2019s delegation-of-authority governance and applicable EU/German law, this transaction is prohibited and blocked.\n\nKEY FINDINGS:\n\u2022 Risk & Compliance: RED ALERT \u2014 Entity is designated on EU, US OFAC SDN, and UK OFSI sanctions lists; credit evaluation halted; critical supply chain blocker requiring immediate PO cancellation.\n\u2022 Tax & Treasury: Theoretical landed cost calculated at \u20ac185,640.00 (invoiced in EUR; 0.00% FX variance); transaction flagged as legally void due to mandatory asset freezes (AWG \u00a7 18) and EU Council Regulation (EU) No 833/2014 Article 3g steel import prohibitions.\n\u2022 IFRS Financial Control: REJECTED \u2014 Appropriately categorized as OpEx under IAS 2 (Inventories, GL 5xxx), exceeding the \u20ac50,000 CFO approval threshold; blocked due to gross regulatory non-compliance.\n\nFINAL DECISION: REJECTED\nReason: Per Aldermoor\u2019s delegation-of-authority matrix, the issuance of a 'RED ALERT' mandates an immediate, non-negotiable rejection due to severe sanctions violations under Council Regulations (EU) No 269/2014 and 833/2014, German Foreign Trade legislation (AWG/AWV), and secondary US sanctions exposure. Global Procurement Head is hereby formally notified of the immediate revocation of purchasing authority for this vendor.\n\nNEXT ACTIONS:\n1. Global Procurement (Head of Procurement) \u2014 Formally cancel Purchase Order with JSC Rosoboronexport and cease all communications \u2014 Immediate (Within 2 hours)\n2. Group Treasury & Accounts Payable \u2014 Enforce an absolute vendor payment freeze and lock vendor master record in the ERP system \u2014 Immediate\n3. Legal & Compliance (General Counsel) \u2014 Document sanctions audit findings for regulatory audit readiness and file requisite disclosures if required under AWG \u2014 By End of Day (18:00 CET)\n4. Strategic Sourcing & Supply Chain Operations \u2014 Initiate emergency re-sourcing for the 40 tonnes of precision steel components from an approved, non-sanctioned European or MFN supplier to mitigate assembly line disruption \u2014 Within 48 hours\n\nSigned,\nCFO Office \u2014 Aldermoor Industries, Hamburg\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T23:55:08.133158Z", "level": "info", "severity": "INFO", "event": "CFO Synthesis complete"}
